Package: sentia-router
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 adduser,
 sentia-base
Recommends: sentia-llama-cpp, sentia-granite-model
Description: Sentia AI router and local inference broker
 The router is the single AI abstraction used by every Sentia application.
 Applications never talk to a model runtime or to a remote vendor directly;
 they speak to the router over a per-user Unix socket.
 .
 The router implements the LOCAL_ONLY, LOCAL_PREFERRED, REMOTE_PREFERRED and
 ASK_BEFORE_REMOTE policies, and falls back to local inference whenever a
 remote provider cannot be used. The local provider is mandatory, so AI
 assistance degrades in quality rather than disappearing.
 .
 This package also ships the peer-authenticated local broker that fronts the
 llama.cpp runtime for the unprivileged sentia-inference system user.

Package: sentia-system-tools
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 polkitd,
 sentia-router (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Structured Sentia system inspection and privileged operations
 Deterministic, typed tools that inspect and modify the system on behalf of
 Sentia. Whenever Linux itself can determine a fact, the fact is measured
 rather than guessed by a language model.
 .
 State-changing operations run through a narrowly authorized system service
 with real polkit authorization. Model output is never executed as shell text
 and a model can never grant its own approval.

Package: sentia-terminal
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 bash (>= 5),
 sentia-router (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Sentia AI-aware terminal and shell integration
 A GTK4/VTE terminal plus Bash integration that adds AI assistance without
 replacing Bash or changing normal command behaviour.
 .
 Provides the ai(1) command for explicit questions, deterministic fuzzy
 matching for command typos, APT metadata search for missing commands and
 optional diagnosis of failed commands. Assistance is configurable down to
 completely off, and a conventional terminal is always available.

Package: sentia-health
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 procps
Recommends: smartmontools, nvme-cli, lm-sensors
Description: Sentia system health monitoring daemon and monitor application
 Efficiently samples CPU, load, memory, swap, filesystem capacity, disk I/O,
 SMART/NVMe health, temperatures, network utilisation, failed systemd units
 and kernel errors using standard lightweight Linux facilities.
 .
 The same metrics are served to the Sentia router tools and to the graphical
 Sentia System Monitor. Nothing is ever deleted or reconfigured automatically
 because a health threshold was crossed.

Package: sentia-providers
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 sentia-router (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Sentia remote AI provider adapters
 Optional adapters that let a user benefit from an AI subscription they
 already pay for, through officially supported vendor interfaces only.
 .
 Each adapter runs in an isolated worker with no access to the user's home
 directory, Sentia runtime sockets or credential stores. Remote providers are
 never required: with none configured, Sentia remains fully functional on the
 local model.

Package: sentia-firstboot
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 sentia-router (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Sentia first-boot setup wizard
 A short, entirely skippable wizard that explains Sentia's offline local AI,
 selects an AI routing policy, offers officially supported remote provider
 integrations and sets privacy and terminal-assistance preferences.
 .
 The wizard works with no Internet connection and requires no account.
